From d133b14c805847a45782504613bba75918fc2f3b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Kofec <18610805+kofec@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 21:21:41 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Enigma2: native hardware for Enigma2 receivers (OpenWebif)

Polls /web/powerstate over HTTP and keeps two devices up to date:

- Unit 1 Status (Media Player): On with the current channel name or
  "Enigma2 ON", Sleeping in standby, Off when the box does not answer
  even ping. A box that pings but whose web interface is silent (Enigma2
  restarting) keeps its last state.
- Unit 2 Source (selector Off|Standby|Reboot|RestartE2|On), mapped to
  /web/powerstate?newstate=. Off sends deep standby when the "Deep
  standby" option is set, otherwise standby.

Settings: address/port, optional HTTP Basic login, poll interval
(Mode1, seconds), deep standby (Mode2), channel name (Mode3).

Devices are looked up by unit, so hardware whose devices were created by
the Enigma2 Python plugin (same units) keeps them, with their history,
when its type is changed to this one.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
